> Measured visits expose the representation cost

The optimized Hopcroft bound depends on efficient inverse transitions,
state-to-block lookup and updating only affected blocks. A smaller-half charging
argument bounds repeated fresh splitter memberships logarithmically, but does
not pay for arbitrary scans of the entire partition. Hopcroft's original
implementation discussion explicitly describes list representations and direct
membership/location information.

This library version stores blocks as ordered sets, constructs predecessor
unions, scans every partition block for each nonempty preimage, and searches the
pending worklist by set equality. Those scans remain even when the preimage is
tiny. With completed n states and k symbols, each proper split increases the
partition count once and appends exactly one additional worklist entry. Thus
pops are at most initial blocks plus proper splits, hence at most n. There are
at most kn symbol passes; each nonempty pass visits all n partition states.
Together with ordered-set insertion/membership and pending comparisons, a
conservative implementation bound is O((k+1)n^2 log(n+1)) time, with O(n(k+1))
ordinary working/output storage. This is not a claim that every input attains
that upper bound.

For the unary threshold family with n at least 8, every state is reachable and
distinguishable. Its actual whole-partition membership count is n^2, while
inverse-transition visits are 2n-2. The next figures plot producing counters and
their normalized values. They replace the old unmeasured n^2-versus-n-log-n
curves; neither curve below represents elapsed time or Moore work. Moore is
checked for the same minimal state count only.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hopcroft_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/dfa_minimization_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <map>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> sizes, scans, inverse, scan_ratio, inverse_ratio;
    std::print("| input states | minimized states | Moore states | pops | proper splits | inverse visits | " "partition-state tests |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256}) {
        const auto input = dm::algorithms::dfa_unary_threshold(n - 1);
        const auto r = dm::algorithms::hopcroft_minimize_run(input);
        const auto moore = dm::algorithms::moore_minimize(input);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n,
                   r.result.num_states, moore.num_states, r.work.splitter_pops,
                   r.work.splits, r.work.predecessor_edges,
                   r.work.partition_states);
        sizes.push_back(n);
        scans.push_back(r.work.partition_states);
        inverse.push_back(r.work.predecessor_edges);
        scan_ratio.push_back(double(r.work.partition_states) / (double(n) * n));
        inverse_ratio.push_back(double(r.work.predecessor_edges) / n);
        if (r.result.num_states != int(n) || moore.num_states != int(n) ||
            r.work.partition_states != n * n ||
            r.work.predecessor_edges != 2 * n - 2)
            throw std::runtime_error("family counters");
    }
    auto left =
        dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), right = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    left.line(sizes, scans, "partition tests", {37, 99, 235}, 2.).line(
        sizes, inverse, "inverse visits", {220, 38, 38}, 2.).title(
        "Actual selected loop visits").x_label("completed states n").y_label(
        "selected visits").y_limits(0, 75000);
    right.line(sizes, scan_ratio, "scans/n^2", {37, 99, 235}, 2.).line(
        sizes, inverse_ratio, "inverse/n", {220, 38, 38}, 2.).title(
        "Normalized actual counts").x_label("completed states n").y_label(
        "normalized visits").y_limits(0, 3);
    auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
    layout.add(left).add(right).size(1250, 620).title("Unary thresholds: set-scanning overhead remains visible").fit_panels().save_svg("build/hopcroft_work.svg");
}
