> Completion, reachability and capture limits

Missing transitions and start=-1 denote an implicit rejecting sink. Completion
materializes one sink only when needed, retaining all original states; therefore
a valid zero-state machine becomes one rejecting state. Refinement includes
unreachable completed states, then quotient BFS drops unreachable blocks. With a
zero-symbol alphabet only epsilon exists, so only the start's acceptance matters
in the returned one-state machine. All-accepting and all-rejecting complete
machines collapse to one reachable state as well.

New run/trace calls default to 100000 completed states and one million completed
transitions, including an added sink and unreachable states. Complete input
validation precedes these policies and graph copies. Zero disables each policy.
Legacy hopcroft_minimize has no optional policy caps. Counts and container sizes
still have representation limits.

Histories own their vectors and add storage beyond the ordinary working/output
bound. Initial capture counts one record per initial block and one ID per
completed state. Every symbol pass adds 1+|A|+|X|; each proper split adds
1+|Y|+|inside|+|outside|. The default one-million-unit cap is admitted online
before history copies once triggering sets are known. It excludes ordinary
working sets, output, metadata and capacity, and is not a byte or peak-memory
limit. A failure throws without returning truncated history; run without capture
ignores this cap. A zero-symbol machine may pop pending blocks while recording
no symbol passes.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hopcroft_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/dfa_minimization_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <map>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    using DFA = dm::algorithms::DFA;
    const std::vector<DFA> inputs = {DFA{}, DFA{1, 1, {{-1}}, 0, {1}},
                                     DFA{3, 1, {{0}, {1}, {2}}, 0, {0, 1, 1}},
                                     DFA{2, 0, {{}, {}}, 1, {0, 1}},
                                     DFA{2, 1, {{1}, {0}}, 0, {1, 1}},
                                     DFA{2, 1, {{1}, {0}}, 0, {0, 0}}};
    const std::vector<std::string> labels = {"empty input", "partial accepting",
                                             "unreachable accepting",
                                             "zero alphabet", "all accepting",
                                             "all rejecting"};
    std::vector<double> x, completed, result;
    std::print("| case | supplied states | completed states | returned reachable states | exact equivalence " "| pops | symbol passes |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < inputs.size(); ++i) {
        const auto t = dm::algorithms::hopcroft_minimize_trace(inputs[i]);
        const bool same =
            dm::algorithms::dfa_equivalence(inputs[i], t.run.result).equivalent;
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", labels[i],
                   inputs[i].num_states, t.run.completed_states,
                   t.run.result.num_states, same, t.run.work.splitter_pops,
                   t.passes.size());
        x.push_back(i + 1);
        completed.push_back(t.run.completed_states);
        result.push_back(t.run.result.num_states);
        if (!same)
            throw std::runtime_error("control language");
    }
    const auto tiny = dm::algorithms::dfa_unary_threshold(2);
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::hopcroft_minimize_trace(tiny);
    const auto exact =
        dm::algorithms::hopcroft_minimize_trace(tiny, {3, 3, t.captured_entries});
    bool history = false, graph = false, domain = false;
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hopcroft_minimize_trace(tiny,
                                                       {3, 3,
                                                        t.captured_entries - 1});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        history = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hopcroft_minimize_run(DFA{1, 1, {{-1}}, 0, {1}},
                                                     {1, 1, 0});
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        graph = true;
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::hopcroft_minimize_run(DFA{2, 1, {{2}, {0}}, 0,
                                                         {0, 0}}, {1, 1, 1});
    } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
        domain = true;
    }
    std::print("\nExact tiny capture units {}; one-short capture rejected {}; projected sink graph rejected " "{}; malformed target rejected before caps {}.\n",
               exact.captured_entries, history, graph, domain);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.points(x, completed, "completed", {37, 99, 235}, 7.).points(
        x, result, "reachable quotient", {220, 38, 38}, 5.).title(
        "Control cases: completion and reachable quotient differ").x_label(
        "case number, following table").y_label("states").y_limits(0, 5).save_svg("build/hopcroft_controls.svg");
    if (!history || !graph || !domain)
        throw std::runtime_error("admission controls");
}
```
